## Follow-up Questions
- How would you translate this into cost-aware testing in a cloud environment?
- What observability signals would you add to detect backpressure when bursts occur?

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates your ability to design realistic performance tests for complex distributed video streaming systems, focusing on real-world ABR streaming scenarios across multiple regions, edge caching effectiveness, and failover resilience under varied network conditions.

## Key Concepts

- ABR streaming SLIs including startup latency, stall density, and bitrate adaptation metrics
- CDN edge caching behavior vs origin server performance and cache warm-up strategies
- Multi-region load shaping techniques and controlled fault injection methodologies
- Autoscaling trigger signals and system resilience patterns for video workloads

## Code Example

```javascript
import http from 'k6/http';
import { sleep } from 'k6';

export default function () {
  http.get('https://edge.example.com/manifest.m3u8');
  sleep(0.5);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adjust test parameters for cold vs warm cache scenarios?
- What strategies would you implement to test CDN edge node failures?
- How do you validate bitrate adaptation algorithms under varying network conditions?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a blend of performance testing craft and real-world data consistency challenges in live collaboration.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end latency and tail behavior in WebSocket paths
- CRDT convergence under bursty edits and network jitter
- Backpressure, throughput budgeting, and backfilling in the event bus
- Soak and chaos testing to reveal bottlenecks and state-sync path risks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo workload generator skeleton
const ws = require('ws');
for (let i=0; i<CLIENTS; i++) {
  const sock = new ws('wss://host/doc');
  sock.on('open', () => {
    setInterval(() => sock.send(JSON.stringify({op:'edit', ...})), EDITS_PER_SEC / 10);
  });
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you instrument CRDT convergence latency vs. message bus throughput?
- How do you validate fairness across regions under skewed latency?
